6. MESSAGE PROTOCOL

Create a transport-independent message format.

A message should contain at minimum:

{
  id,
  conversationId,
  senderId,
  senderDeviceId,
  type,
  ciphertext,
  createdAt,
  ttl,
  hopCount,
  maxHops,
  replyTo,
  attachmentId,
  signature,
  status,
  protocolVersion
}


Requirements:

id must be globally unique.
Generate IDs locally.
Never depend on a Supabase database ID.
Messages must be serializable.
Messages must be validated before processing.
Messages must contain a protocol version.
Unknown/invalid messages must be rejected safely.
7. OFFLINE-FIRST BEHAVIOR

Sending a message should follow:

User
 ↓
Create Message
 ↓
Encrypt
 ↓
Persist Locally
 ↓
Add to Outbox
 ↓
Select Available Transport


If Internet is available:

Supabase


If Internet is unavailable on mobile:

BLE Mesh


If transmission fails:

Outbox
 ↓
Retry


The UI must not fail simply because Supabase is unavailable.

8. LOCAL STORAGE

Implement proper local persistence.

For Web:

IndexedDB or another appropriate browser database.

For Mobile:

SQLite or another reliable persistent database.

Do not use localStorage as the primary database for messages.

Persist:

messages
conversations
outbox
processed message IDs
sync state
device identity
encryption metadata
9. MESSAGE DEDUPLICATION

Mesh networks can deliver the same message multiple times.

Implement deduplication based on:

message.id


Before processing:

if message already processed:
    ignore
else:
    process


The same message must never appear multiple times in the UI.

10. MESH RELAY

Support multi-hop messaging:

A
 ↓
B
 ↓
C
 ↓
D


If B receives a message intended for D, B may relay it.

Use:

hopCount
maxHops
messageId
TTL


Example:

maxHops = 7


Increment:

hopCount++


Stop relaying when:

hopCount >= maxHops


Prevent infinite loops.

Never continuously rebroadcast the same message.

11. STORE & FORWARD

Support temporary message storage.

When a device receives a message:

Receive
 ↓
Validate
 ↓
Deduplicate
 ↓
Store temporarily
 ↓
Relay if appropriate


Implement:

TTL
expiration
maximum cache size
deduplication
cleanup

Do not allow unlimited storage.

